2026-09-27T07:22:17.5566857Z Description:
2026-09-27T07:22:17.5567427Z This PPA contains more recent Python versions packaged for Ubuntu.
2026-09-27T07:22:17.5567955Z 
2026-09-27T07:22:17.5569355Z Disclaimer: there's no guarantee of timely updates in case of security problems or other issues. If you want to use them in a security-or-otherwise-critical environment (say, on a production server), you do so at your own risk.
2026-09-27T07:22:17.5570733Z 
2026-09-27T07:22:17.5570867Z Update Note
2026-09-27T07:22:17.5571150Z ===========
2026-09-27T07:22:17.5571574Z Please use this repository instead of ppa:fkrull/deadsnakes.
2026-09-27T07:22:17.5571973Z 
2026-09-27T07:22:17.5572101Z Reporting Issues
2026-09-27T07:22:17.5572416Z ================
2026-09-27T07:22:17.5572600Z 
2026-09-27T07:22:17.5572840Z Issues can be reported in the master issue tracker at:
2026-09-27T07:22:17.5573391Z https://github.com/deadsnakes/issues/issues
2026-09-27T07:22:17.5573826Z 
2026-09-27T07:22:17.5574124Z Supported Ubuntu and Python Versions
2026-09-27T07:22:17.5574536Z ====================================
2026-09-27T07:22:17.5574795Z 
2026-09-27T07:22:17.5575297Z - Ubuntu 22.04 (jammy) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.10)
2026-09-27T07:22:17.5575970Z - Ubuntu 24.04 (noble) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.12)
2026-09-27T07:22:17.5576652Z - Ubuntu 26.04 (resolute) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.14)
2026-09-27T07:22:17.5577811Z - Note: Python 3.10 (jammy), Python3.12 (noble), Python3.14 (resolute) are not provided by deadsnakes as upstream ubuntu provides those packages.
2026-09-27T07:22:17.5578827Z 
2026-09-27T07:22:17.5581269Z Why some packages aren't built:
2026-09-27T07:22:17.5582445Z - Note: for 22.04+, older python versions requre libssl<3 so they are not currently built
2026-09-27T07:22:17.5583515Z - If you need these, reach out to asottile to set up a private ppa
2026-09-27T07:22:17.5584006Z 
2026-09-27T07:22:17.5584533Z The packages may also work on other versions of Ubuntu or Debian, but that is not tested or supported.
2026-09-27T07:22:17.5585516Z 
2026-09-27T07:22:17.5585694Z Packages
2026-09-27T07:22:17.5586075Z ========
2026-09-27T07:22:17.5586269Z 
2026-09-27T07:22:17.5588886Z The packages provided here are loosely based on the debian upstream packages with some modifications to make them more usable as non-default pythons and on ubuntu.  As such, the packages follow debian's patterns and often do not include a full python distribution with just `apt install python#.#`.  Here is a list of packages that may be useful along with the default install:
2026-09-27T07:22:17.5591385Z 
2026-09-27T07:22:17.5591764Z - `python#.#-dev`: includes development headers for building C extensions
2026-09-27T07:22:17.5592581Z - `python#.#-venv`: provides the standard library `venv` module
2026-09-27T07:22:17.5662314Z - `python#.#-distutils`: provides the standard library `distutils` module
2026-09-27T07:22:17.5663586Z - `python#.#-lib2to3`: provides the `2to3-#.#` utility as well as the standard library `lib2to3` module
2026-09-27T07:22:17.5664618Z - `python#.#-gdbm`: provides the standard library `dbm.gnu` module
2026-09-27T07:22:17.5665394Z - `python#.#-tk`: provides the standard library `tkinter` module
2026-09-27T07:22:17.5665710Z 
2026-09-27T07:22:17.5666037Z Third-Party Python Modules
2026-09-27T07:22:17.5666282Z ==========================
2026-09-27T07:22:17.5666428Z 
2026-09-27T07:22:17.5667448Z Python modules in the official Ubuntu repositories are packaged to work with the Python interpreters from the official repositories. Accordingly, they generally won't work with the Python interpreters from this PPA. As an exception, pure-Python modules for Python 3 will work, but any compiled extension modules won't.
2026-09-27T07:22:17.5668594Z 
2026-09-27T07:22:17.5669218Z To install 3rd-party Python modules, you should use the common Python packaging tools.  For an introduction into the Python packaging ecosystem and its tools, refer to the Python Packaging User Guide:
2026-09-27T07:22:17.5670058Z https://packaging.python.org/installing/
2026-09-27T07:22:17.5670275Z 
